### 📝 Executive Summary

XGBoost is an end-to-end scalable gradient tree boosting system that has gained widespread adoption across competitive machine learning benchmarks and enterprise data pipelines. The paper introduces novel algorithms for sparse data handling, a weighted quantile sketch for approximate tree learning, cache-aware block structure design, and out-of-core processing capabilities. These innovations allow XGBoost to scale to billions of examples while using drastically fewer resources than existing systems.

---

